      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0091",
      "sequence": 946,
      "meaning": "Enraged by Rāma’s answer, Rāvaṇa releases thunderbolt-like arrows of every form until sky and quarters are covered. Rāma answers with fire-arrows that burn them in an instant and turns the demon’s fierce spear back with one of his shafts. He effortlessly cuts apart millions of discs, tridents and other weapons; all Rāvaṇa’s arrows fail like every desire of the wicked. Rāvaṇa then strikes Mātali with a hundred arrows. The charioteer falls crying victory to Rāma; the Lord graciously raises him and enters supreme wrath.",
