      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0092",
      "sequence": 947,
      "meaning": "Rāma’s winged, serpent-like arrows first kill Rāvaṇa’s driver and horses, smash the chariot and strike down its standard. His inner strength failing, Rāvaṇa roars and immediately mounts another chariot, releasing weapons by many arts, all fruitless like the designs of one bent on harming others. Ten tridents bring Rāma’s four horses to earth; the Lord raises them and fires. His bee-like shafts enter the lotus grove of Rāvaṇa’s heads, ten arrows piercing each forehead so streams of blood flow. Thirty more cut down heads with their arms, but whenever Rāma severs them new ones instantly grow. He repeatedly cuts the heads and arms in divine sport until the sky is crowded as though with countless comets and Rāhus.",
