    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0093",
      "sequence": 948,
      "meaning": "Seeing his heads multiply, the ten-headed demon forgets death and grows fiercely angry. Drawing all ten bows, he blankets Rāma’s chariot with arrows until it disappears for a whole moment like the sun hidden in fog. When the gods cry out, Rāma angrily takes his bow, counters the shafts and cuts off the enemy’s heads, filling every direction of the sky. Flying along the aerial paths, the severed heads shout victory and terrifyingly call for Lakṣmaṇa, Sugrīva and Raghubīra.",
