    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0094",
      "sequence": 949,
      "meaning": "Seeing a dreadful spear coming toward Vibhīṣaṇa, Rāma—whose vow is to end the distress of those who surrender—moves his friend behind him and receives the missile upon himself. He briefly swoons in deliberate divine play, distressing the gods. Seeing the Lord appear weary, Vibhīṣaṇa charges with his mace and denounces Rāvaṇa as wretched, foolish and opposed to gods, humans, sages and nāgas. The millions of heads once respectfully offered to Śiva have preserved him until now, he says, but death dances above him: one estranged from Rāma cannot possess prosperity. He strikes Rāvaṇa in the chest.",
