      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0095",
      "sequence": 950,
      "meaning": "Seeing Vibhīṣaṇa exhausted, Hanumān charges carrying a mountain. He brings down Rāvaṇa’s chariot, horses and driver and kicks him in the chest, leaving him upright but trembling while Vibhīṣaṇa returns to the protector of creatures. Challenged by Rāvaṇa, Hanumān leaps into the sky with tail extended. The demon seizes it and rises with him; the two mighty fighters grapple in the air, striking each other in wrath and looking like a mountain of lampblack battling golden Sumeru. Unable to find the limit of Rāvaṇa’s guile and strength, the son of the Wind remembers his Lord.",
