      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0096",
      "sequence": 951,
      "meaning": "Rāvaṇa vanishes for a moment and reappears in innumerable forms: as many ten-headed demons manifest throughout the field as there are bears and monkeys in Rāma’s army. Seeing them everywhere, the allies lose courage, flee and cry out to Lakṣmaṇa and Raghubīra. Millions of Rāvaṇas race through all ten directions with dreadful roars. The terrified gods abandon hope of victory and urge one another to hide in mountain caves, for one ten-headed demon conquered them all and now has become many. Only Brahmā, Śiva and sages who know something of the Lord’s greatness remain.",
