      "sequence": 952,
      "meaning": "In an instant the Lord cuts away the entire illusion as sunrise tears apart darkness. The gods rejoice to see only one Rāvaṇa and again shower flowers. Rāma raises his arms and rallies the monkeys, who call to one another and rush back into battle with agile fury. Seeing the gods praising Rāma, Rāvaṇa shouts that they have always been his beaten slaves and charges into the sky. The gods flee in panic; Aṅgada springs after the villain, seizes his feet and throws him to earth.",
