    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0099",
      "sequence": 954,
      "meaning": "That night Trijaṭā visits Sītā and recounts the battle. Hearing that Rāvaṇa’s severed heads and arms grow back, Sītā is deeply afraid and asks how the world’s tormentor can die when Raghupati’s arrows cannot kill him. She blames her misfortune and the hostile Fate that fashioned the false golden deer, caused her to speak harshly to Lakṣmaṇa and has kept alive the one who separated her from Hari’s lotus feet. Rāma’s absence strikes her repeatedly like a poisoned arrow. Trijaṭā consoles her: the enemy will die when a shaft strikes his heart, but the Lord does not yet pierce it because Vaidehī dwells there.",
