    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0100",
      "sequence": 955,
      "meaning": "After consoling Sītā in many ways, Trijaṭā returns home. Remembering Rāma’s nature, Vaidehī is overwhelmed by separation; she reproaches night and moon, and the night seems an age long. When the burning in her heart becomes extreme, her left eye and arm throb. Reading the omen, she steadies herself in hope of meeting compassionate Raghubīra. At midnight Rāvaṇa awakens and angrily berates his charioteer for removing him from battle. The driver clasps his feet and reasons with him; at dawn Rāvaṇa mounts again. News of his approach throws the monkey host into turmoil, and champions uproot mountains and trees and charge gnashing their teeth.",
